  "notes": "Complete Louisville ornamental WaterTower/Q3263909 and associated original1860white PumpingStationNo1/WaterWorksMuseum: original17vertexcircular towerbaseway332331161 and complete36vertexpumphouse/wingsway332331169, separate intrinsic structures at actualnativepositions, no connecting site slab. Tower has circular open ten-column lower colonnade/cornice, open balustrade/ten statuepedestals and ten representative zinc human sculptures with varied draped/standing poses including visible hunter/dog/raised-arm/waterpouring figures, tall tapered ribbed/paneled pale castiron shaft, large uppercapital, slotted lantern and ribbed domedcap/finial. Pumphouse has tall central Greektempleblock/front columns/pediment, lower attached symmetricalwings/endpavilions/pilasters/smallpediments/dressed recessed sash/entries/slate roofs and hidden rear wall offsets. No detached later yellow/Romanesque pumping halls/chimneys/adjacent buildings/river/landscape/plaza/roads/powerpylons/people/flags/lettering/interiors."
